 Inventory I/O or identity failure is explicit and never deletes the retained
 tree. Unresolved ownership keeps the existing leases and project intact; its
 record is `ownership-unresolved`, with no racing inventory of an active project.
+Inventory traversal uses descriptor-relative directory enumeration, stat and
+no-follow opens; nested enumeration/stat/read errors propagate rather than
+silently omitting a subtree. Only verified initial absence is `missing`.
+An inventory failure sets `inventory-incomplete` and fails an otherwise
+successful transaction. If the build was already failing, that original error
+retains precedence and the additional retention failure is reported separately.
 
 This flag is local-only. The remote wrapper still forwards arguments, but the
 driver rejects `--retain-project` for a remote backend before dispatch; remote
